    "notes": "llama.cpp release b11071 (commit 6ad1af56033cc9d4cecacf574ac8af8eb4b3249e) built from source on the box: cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DGGML_CUDA=ON -DGGML_CUDA_GRAPHS=ON -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=121, GNU 13.3.0, CUDA 13.0, driver 580.173.02, Ubuntu 24.04.4, kernel 6.17.0-1029-nvidia. Weights: badtheorylabs/Tinfield-1-Compact-GGUF at revision 79689f3f, the six IQ2XXS shards (77,363,822,656 bytes), sha256 checked against the Hub. Served with GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=1 and: llama-server -m tinfield-1-compact-IQ2XXS-00001-of-00006.gguf --alias tinfield -ngl 999 -fa on -b 2048 -ub 2048 -t 20 --jinja --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 -c 262144 -np 1 --load-mode none -n 16384. That is one slot of 262144 tokens, the native context, f16 K and V cache, the whole file read into memory instead of memory-mapped. Load to /health took 44-50 s; the server process held about 94 GB of the 121 GiB unified memory with 27 GB still available. The sampler flags are the model card values and only matter for requests that set none; every request here sets temperature 0 and seed 42. The chat template defaults to thinking on with reasoning_effort xhigh and preserves earlier turns reasoning (llama.cpp enables reasoning-preserve by default for it). Speed rows turn thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false; eval rows use the template default."
